-- title:
--   Flat unramified ascent of regularity and of the parameters (varpi,s)
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a regular local ring and $O'$ a noetherian local ring, given as an $O$-algebra whose structure map $O \to O'$ is a local homomorphism, with $O'$ flat as an $O$-module, essentially of finite type over $O$, and unramified over $O$ at the maximal ideal of $O'$. Assume there are elements $\varpi, s \in O$ with $\mathfrak m_O = (\varpi, s)$, that $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} O = 2$, and that $O/(s)$ is a discrete valuation ring in the following form: there is a discrete valuation ring $D$ (a domain) and a surjective ring homomorphism $\pi : O \to D$ with $\ker \pi = (s)$. The conclusion is fourfold: $O'$ is a regular local ring; $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} O' = 2$; the maximal ideal of $O'$ is generated by the images of $\varpi$ and $s$ under $O \to O'$; the ideal of $O'$ generated by the image of $s$ is prime; and, witnessing that $O'$ modulo that ideal is a domain, the quotient $O'/(s)$ is a discrete valuation ring. Thus all of the data $(\mathfrak m = (\varpi,s)$, dimension $2$, $s$ prime with DVR quotient$)$ ascends along the extension.
--
--   This is the ascent of regularity and of a chosen pair of regular parameters along a flat, essentially finite type extension that is unramified at the closed point, in the non-complete form (compare the analogous statement for étale extensions). It is used in proving regularity of fibres of modular curves at full level, where the two-dimensional regular local data together with the prime divisor $s$ is transported along a map that is unramified away from a section.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_flat_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair.lean

